{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"68","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Contact"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"3 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Little Petya is preparing for the first contact with aliens. He knows that alien spaceships have shapes of non-degenerate triangles and there will be exactly 4 ships. Landing platform for a ship can be made of 3 special columns located at some points of a Cartesian plane such that these 3 points form a triangle equal to the ship with respect to rotations, translations (parallel shifts along some vector) and reflections (symmetries along the edges). The ships can overlap after the landing."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each column can be used to land more than one ship, for example, if there are two equal ships, we don't need to build 6 columns to land both ships, 3 will be enough. Petya wants to know what minimum number of columns will be enough to land all ships. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of 4 lines will contain 6 integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x1"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x2"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y2"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x3"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y3"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3 ≤ 20"},{"kind":"text","text":"), representing 3 points that describe the shape of each of 4 ships. It is guaranteed that 3 points in each line will represent a non-degenerate triangle."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First line should contain minimum number of columns enough to land all spaceships."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0 1 0 1 2\n0 0 0 2 2 2\n0 0 3 0 1 2\n0 0 3 0 2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0 0 0 1 1 1\n0 0 0 2 2 2\n0 0 0 5 5 5\n0 0 0 17 17 17\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"9\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case columns can be put in these points: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0), (1, 0), (3, 0), (1, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note that the second ship can land using last 3 columns."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case following points can be chosen: "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 0), (0, 1), (1, 0), (0, 2), (2, 0), (0, 5), (5, 0), (0, 17), (17, 0)"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is impossible to use less than 9 columns."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"68E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/68/problem/E"}